# Git Workflow Rules

Before starting any coding task, always remind the user to pull the latest code from Git so the local project has the newest content and changes.

Recommended starting commands:

```bash
git status
git branch
git pull origin main
```

If the project uses another branch, check the current branch first and pull from that branch.

Rules:
- Never work on outdated code if Git is available.
- Never overwrite other people's work.
- Never force push.
- Never delete files unless clearly requested.
- Do not commit or push unless the user asks.
- After changes, summarize the files changed.

Before finishing a task, suggest running:

```bash
git status
npm run build
```

Use the correct build command from package.json if it is different.
